    "title": "People's Law School offers free course on legal topics - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Stan Boney ,\n1 hours ago\nBOARDMAN, Ohio (WKBN) – Twenty years ago, Lynn Maro ran the People’s Law School as part of the Mahoning County Bar Association. Now that Maro is the county prosecutor, she has decided to resurrect the law school.\nThe first of five, two-hour sessions was held on Wednesday evening at Boardman Library. They will continue for the next four weeks — starting at 5:30 p.m. — all in Boardman.\nWednesday evening’s lessons were about criminal prosecution and plea bargaining, along with misdemeanors and OVI.\n“Then, next week, we’re going to do a segment on human trafficking. We have a Grace Court that Judge Disalvo offers. She’ll be speaking about that. We’ll have someone from the task force speaking about the sting operations we see in the news a lot,” Maro said.\nThere will also be sessions on constitutional law, landlord-tenant issues and probate cases.\nNinety people registered to attend, which was more than Maro anticipated. Registration is required for future sessions.\nInformation on the sessions and registration is available on the prosecutor’s website or the library’s website.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKBN.com.",
